    "q-181641": {
      "dom_id": "step-q181641",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Which of the following sets are infinite?\n\n- $A={{f}^{(n)}(x)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}({e}^{1-2x})\\,:\\,n\\in {N}_{0}}$\n- $B={{g}^{(n)}(x)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}(3{e}^{x})\\,:\\,n\\in {N}_{0}}$\n- $C={{h}^{(n)}(x)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}(4{e}^{-x})\\,:\\,n\\in {N}_{0}}$",
      "worked_solution": "The cardinality of a finite set is the number of elements contained within it. A set is infinite if it has infinitely many elements.\n\n- The set $A$ is infinite. Listing the first few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{(0)}(x) & ={e}^{1-2x} \\\\ {f}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{1-2x})=-2{e}^{1-2x} \\\\ {f}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2{e}^{1-2x})=4{e}^{1-2x} \\\\ {f}^{(3)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{e}^{1-2x})=-8{e}^{1-2x} \\\\ ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\nA={{e}^{1-2x},-2{e}^{1-2x},4{e}^{1-2x},-8{e}^{1-2x},…}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $A$ is infinite.\n\n- The set $B$ is finite. Listing the first few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{(0)}(x) & =3{e}^{x} \\\\ {g}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{e}^{x})=3{e}^{x} \\\\ {g}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{e}^{x})=3{e}^{x} \\\\ {g}^{(3)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{e}^{x})=3{e}^{x} \\\\ ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $B$ contains only one element:\n\n$$\nB={3{e}^{x}}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $|B|=1,$ which is finite.\n\n- The set $C$ is finite. Listing the first few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{(0)}(x) & =4{e}^{-x} \\\\ {h}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{e}^{-x})=-4{e}^{-x} \\\\ {h}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4{e}^{-x})=4{e}^{-x} \\\\ {h}^{(3)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{e}^{-x})=-4{e}^{-x} \\\\ ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $C$ contains only two elements:\n\n$$\nC={4{e}^{-x},-4{e}^{-x}}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $|C|=2,$ which is finite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
