    "q-181652": {
      "dom_id": "step-q181652",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Which of the following sets are infinite?\n\n- $A={{f}^{(n)}(x)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,:\\,n\\in {N}_{0}}$\n- $B={{g}^{(n)}(x)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)\\,:\\,n\\in {N}_{0}}$\n- $C={{h}^{(n)}(x)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,:\\,n\\in {N}_{0}}$",
      "worked_solution": "The cardinality of a finite set is the number of elements contained within it. A set is infinite if it has infinitely many elements.\n\n- The set $A$ is infinite. Listing the first few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{(0)}(x) & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({sec}^{2}⁡x)=2{sec}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\nA={\\operatorname{tan}⁡x,{sec}^{2}⁡x,2{sec}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x,…}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $A$ is infinite.\n\n- The set $B$ is also infinite. Listing the first few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{(0)}(x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x \\\\ {g}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x \\\\ {g}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)=-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x \\\\ {g}^{(3)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)=-27\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x \\\\ ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\nB={\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x,-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x,-27\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x,…}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B$ is infinite.\n\n- The set $C$ is finite. Listing the first few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{(0)}(x) & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {h}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {h}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {h}^{(3)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {h}^{(4)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $C$ contains four elements:\n\n$$\nC={3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $|C|=4,$ which is finite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ and $B$ only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
